From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mowsoon <Mowsoon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] workspace: don't log a critical error while the session
 is inactive

When the session is inactive, for example while another VT is in the
foreground during a suspend, the DRM backend refuses output changes with
OutputErrorCode::NotActive. updateOutputConfiguration() already treats
that as expected and waits for the next VT switch, which applies the
configuration again, but it still logs "Applying output configuration
failed" at critical level.

On a system with two GPUs, logind resumes the devices one after the
other when the session becomes active again. The first resumed GPU
triggers updateOutputConfiguration() while the GPU that drives the
outputs is still inactive, so the critical message is logged on every
resume from suspend or hibernation, and when the session ends at
shutdown, although the outputs come back as configured.

At login, the greeter hands the GPUs over to the user session. The
compositor of the greeter has already lost DRM master when it applies
its last configuration, and the backend answers NoPermission instead.

Log the NotActive and NoPermission cases at debug level and keep the
critical message for real failures.
---
diff --git a/src/workspace.cpp b/src/workspace.cpp
--- a/src/workspace.cpp
+++ b/src/workspace.cpp
@@ -714,7 +714,12 @@
         }
     } while (result.error().code != OutputErrorCode::NotActive && !toEnable.isEmpty() && !alreadyHaveEnabledOutputs);
 
-    qCCritical(KWIN_CORE, "Applying output configuration failed: %s", qPrintable(result.error().message));
+    if (result.error().code == OutputErrorCode::NotActive || result.error().code == OutputErrorCode::NoPermission) {
+        // the configuration gets applied again once the session is active
+        qCDebug(KWIN_CORE, "Not applying output configuration while the session is inactive");
+    } else {
+        qCCritical(KWIN_CORE, "Applying output configuration failed: %s", qPrintable(result.error().message));
+    }
     // Update the output order to a fallback list, to avoid dangling pointers
     updateOutputOrder();
     // If applying the output configuration failed, brightness devices weren't assigned either.
